[2026-09-21 15:12:43 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 111]   Step 111 -- detachment-cut coherence of the resident axis.
[2026-09-21 15:12:43 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 111]   The resident signature is measured on one selection: a>150 AU,
[2026-09-21 15:12:43 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 111]   q>30 AU, condition code <=3 (step 010).  Steps 023 and 080
[2026-09-21 15:12:43 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 111]   stress-test that cell -- jackknife, era, orbit quality, newest
[2026-09-21 15:12:43 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 111]   cohort -- but every one of those tests holds the detachment
[2026-09-21 15:12:43 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 111]   boundary fixed.  A referee's sharper question is whether the
[2026-09-21 15:12:43 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 111]   recovered DIRECTION is a property of the detached population or
[2026-09-21 15:12:43 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 111]   an artefact of one cut: if the same axis is recovered across the
[2026-09-21 15:12:43 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 111]   whole family of (a_min, q_min) criteria, the direction belongs to
[2026-09-21 15:12:43 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 111]   the population; if it wanders with the cut, it belongs to the
[2026-09-21 15:12:43 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 111]   selection.
[2026-09-21 15:12:43 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 111]   This step scans the detachment plane:
[2026-09-21 15:12:43 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 111]   T1  for each cell of a_min in {100,125,150,175,200,225,250} AU
[2026-09-21 15:12:43 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 111]   crossed with q_min in {30,33,35,38,40,45,50} AU (cc<=3), the
[2026-09-21 15:12:43 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 111]   varpi Rayleigh significance under the identical conditioned
[2026-09-21 15:12:43 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 111]   null (fix a,e,i; uniform node and argument of perihelion)
[2026-09-21 15:12:43 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 111]   T2  for each cell, the 3-D perihelion-direction resultant and its
[2026-09-21 15:12:43 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 111]   ecliptic (lam,beta) -- and the angular separation of that
[2026-09-21 15:12:43 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 111]   recovered direction from the declared detached-sample axis
[2026-09-21 15:12:43 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 111]   (49.9,-17)
[2026-09-21 15:12:43 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 111]   T3  coherence summary: the fraction of adequately sized cells
[2026-09-21 15:12:43 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 111]   whose recovered direction lands within 20/30/40 deg of the
[2026-09-21 15:12:43 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 111]   axis, the circular dispersion of the per-cell recovered
[2026-09-21 15:12:43 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 111]   varpi means about the declared 49.1 deg, and whether the
[2026-09-21 15:12:43 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 111]   declared cell sits inside the coherent plateau or on its
[2026-09-21 15:12:43 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 111]   edge.
[2026-09-21 15:12:43 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 111]   Cells with fewer than 8 objects are recorded but excluded from
[2026-09-21 15:12:43 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 111]   the coherence fractions.  Cells are nested (the a>250 sample is
[2026-09-21 15:12:43 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 111]   a subset of a>150), so the map measures direction coherence, not
[2026-09-21 15:12:43 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 111]   independent replication.
