[2026-09-21 15:12:44 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 111] verdict: Across 42 adequately sized detachment cuts the recovered direction is coherent, not cut-specific: 74 per cent of cells recover a perihelion direction within 30 deg of the detached-sample axis, and 100 per cent land within 30 deg of one of the two declared directions.  The direction drifts systematically with detachment depth -- from the detached axis (49.9,-17) at shallow cuts toward the cap-declaration direction (34,-13) at the deepest cells, several of which land within 0.4-12 deg of the cap axis -- so the population recovers the sector the two declared directions bracket rather than a single point.  34/42 cells are significant under the conditioned null; the declared a>150, q>30 cell sits inside the coherent plateau.  The axis is a property of the detached population, not an artefact of the selection boundary.
